WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.470
With a legendary career spanning nearly 60
years, Jack Nicholson is considered one of

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.339
Hollywood's all-time greats.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.810
But the award-winning actor hasn't appeared
in a movie since 2010, meaning fans only get

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.030
to see him when he pops up at award shows.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.620
So what's up with the actor's disappearance?

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.400
Well, if you think you can handle the truth,
keep on watching to find out why we don't

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.920
hear from Jack Nicholson anymore.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.120
His last film was a bomb

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:26.260
Nicholson's last film, 2010's How Do You Know,
should have been great.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:30.619
It boasted an all-star cast including Paul
Rudd, Reese Witherspoon and Owen Wilson while

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:34.340
reuniting Nicholson with Terms of Endearment
and As Good As It Gets writer and director

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.400
James L. Brooks.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.700
However, the film was a critical failure and
a box office bomb, earning just over $48 million

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.700
worldwide against a budget of $120 million.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.620
At the age of 80, Nicholson has to really
want to be in a film these days to bother

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.830
- and with his last movie being such a disappointing
experience, it's no wonder he's shied away

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.120
from movies ever since.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.440
"You do not have the luxury of not hearing
this"

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.920
"God are you gonna make me literally run from
bad news?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.140
"The board has dec-..."

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.900
Memory loss

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.900
Long gaps between films is actually nothing
new for Nicholson.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.420
As he's gotten older, he's frequently taken
long breaks between movies while waiting for

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:14.380
the right project to come along, with four
years transpiring between As Good As It Gets

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.670
and The Pledge, and three years between Something's
Gotta Give and The Departed.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:23.250
But in 2013, rumors began swirling that his
current break wasn't caused by a lack of interest,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:27.550
but instead by the rigors of old age, as Radar
Online reported that Nicholson was suffering

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.440
from memory loss.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.590
A source told the tabloid "Jack has memory
issues and can no longer remember the lines

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.460
being asked of him."

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.040
Not so fast

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.670
Reports of Nicholson's supposed memory loss
immediately went viral, sparking a debate

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.350
in the media over whether the allegations
were true.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:45.909
Just a few weeks later, however, a pretty
reliable source came forward saying that Nicholson

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:47.040
was doing just fine.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.080
That source?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.200
Nicholson himself.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.890
Yep, Nicholson sat down for a rare interview
with The Sun and explained that his memory

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:54.720
is
totally fine.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.820
Instead, he chalked up the reason for his
absence to simple boredom with the whole movie

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.560
star thing, saying he was enjoying the retired
life.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.760
“I’m not going to work until the day I
die, that’s not why I started this.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.390
I mean, I’m not driven.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.729
I was driven — but I’m not, I don’t
have to be out there any more.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.209
In fact, there’s part of me that never really
liked being out there.

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:14.220
[...] I don’t enjoy it, simple as that.”

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.480
And that certainly has the ring of truth.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.490
"you want answers?"

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.560
"I think I'm entitled to it."

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.480
"You want answers?"

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.740
"I want the truth!"

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.600
"You can't handle the truth!"

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.840
Don't call it a comeback

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.660
Given his legendary status, you'd think Nicholson
would pretty much have his pick of movie roles.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.300
And you're right.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.580
In just the past few years, Nicholson has
reportedly turned down offers to appear in

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:38.750
films like The Judge, 42, and Nebraska, with
those roles instead going to Robert Duvall,

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.200
Harrison Ford, and Bruce Dern.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.370
He was also involved in St. Vincent before
recommending Bill Murray for the role instead,

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:49.050
and his pal Warren Beatty tried to get him
to star in Rules Don't Apply with no luck.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.770
But his acting days might not be entirely
behind him just yet.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:55.270
According to Variety, Nicholson is planning
to return to the big screen for a remake of

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:59.430
the German comedy Toni Erdmann, which earned
an Oscar nomination for Best Foreign Feature.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.190
Of course, he's changed his mind before, but
here's hoping we get to see Jack doing his

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.980
thing on screen at least one more time.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.620
"Here's Johnny!"

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.160
And if not?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.780
Well, considering that Nicholson has appeared
in some of the greatest films of all time,

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.569
and given us some of the most indelible roles
in movie history, it's clear he has nothing

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:19.280
left to prove to anyone - least of all himself.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.660
All we can say is, thanks, Jack.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.319
Thanks for watching!

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.510
